4. INTENDED RELICENSING OF THE DISCLOSURE PACKAGE

   The `disclosure/` directory contains `privity-disclosure`, a standalone Daml
   package with no fund or settlement logic in it, designed so that any Canton
   application can depend on it.

   It is released under these terms during the HackCanton Season 3 competition
   period only. After the competition concludes, the intent is to relicense
   `privity-disclosure` under Apache-2.0 so that it can be adopted freely as an
   ecosystem primitive.

   The reason for the delay is narrow and stated plainly: a competing entry in
   the same track works on adjacent tokenized-fund infrastructure, and handing
   over a ready-made component mid-competition is not something this licence
   will do. Judges, reviewers and anyone else evaluating the work have full
   rights under section 1 in the meantime.

   Any relicensing will be recorded with its boundary commit and its date.
   Relicensing operates forward only: anyone who obtained a copy under these
   terms keeps those terms and owes nothing.

